# Personal Branding Agent — scheduled triggers (PLAN.md Step 12)
#
# Cron was chosen over a systemd timer for this deployment:
#
# * one user, one machine, fixed coarse intervals (twice weekly / 24h) — no
#   second granularity, no unit dependencies, no journal integration needed;
# * one file versus two services plus two timers plus daemon-reload plus
#   lingering for user timers;
# * cron works without a running systemd init (containers, minimal installs),
#   while a timer file is dead weight there;
# * exit status surfaces through cron directly, and output is captured in the
#   gitignored logs/ directory below.
#
# Revisit for systemd timers if any of that changes (finer granularity,
# dependency ordering, or structured journal logging become requirements).
#
# Install (after setting PROJECT_ROOT to the checkout path):
#
#     crontab ops/personal-branding-agent.cron
#
# The scheduler only triggers; the workflows execute. Each line runs the
# Step 11 entry point once and exits with its status: 0 success (including a
# run that published nothing or one post), 1 failed run, 2 needs a person,
# 3 rejected without running (workflow already locked). No masking constructs
# (`|| true`, `; exit 0`) may be added here — a scheduled failure must stay
# visible outside the application.

PROJECT_ROOT=/home/alaabadawii/LLMs/IBM/Build_RAG_Applications_Get_Started/PersonalBrandingAgent

# Branding pipeline, twice weekly: Tuesday and Friday at 10:00.
# The schedule is interpreted in the daemon's timezone, which is the system
# timezone (Africa/Cairo on this host). cron 3.0pl1 has no CRON_TZ support and
# ignores a crontab TZ= for scheduling, so the time is local by definition.
0 10 * * 2,5 cd "$PROJECT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python -m app.workflows.branding >> "$PROJECT_ROOT/logs/branding-cron.log" 2>&1

# Knowledge synchronization, daily at 02:10.
10 2 * * * cd "$PROJECT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python -m app.workflows.sync >> "$PROJECT_ROOT/logs/sync-cron.log" 2>&1
